# Where a tutorial note stands for a point of the screen (see tutwin.c, tutwin_place): the points here are given to tut_win itself (the
# way the tour's helpers do), so the popup goes to the side and the height the point asks for, not to the first unit's square's. A point
# low on the screen puts the popup at an eighth of its y with the arrow from the popup's bottom edge; one high up puts it at the bottom
# of the screen. Right of the middle puts it at the right. The last are modes 3, 4 and 5 with the point under their limits, and one
# note has a second arrow. Return closes each.
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
44 open tut_at_low_right
50 snap low-right
52 key Return
56 open tut_at_low_left
62 snap low-left
64 key Return
68 open tut_at_high_right
74 snap high-right
76 key Return
80 open tut_at_second
86 snap second-arrow
88 key Return
92 open tut_at_m3_low
98 snap m3-low
100 key Return
104 open tut_at_m4_low
110 snap m4-low
112 key Return
116 open tut_at_m5_low
122 snap m5-low
124 key Return
128 snap closed
130 close
# The base screen can open under the notes (Return reaches the game too): its leader portraits (and a pixel at the left panel's corner) animate slower than a snap's burst.
mask 265 625 310 680
mask 700 625 760 680
mask 134 709 138 713
